{"thought":"The test I created passed, which indicates that the `do_first` function is currently pickleable, contrary to the issue description. This suggests that the decorator might not be affecting the function as expected in this commit. I will modify the test to check the `__name__` and `__qualname__` attributes of the `do_first` function instead, as this is the core of the issue. I will write a new test to verify that these attributes are incorrect, which should fail due to the bug.","final_test":"import pytest
import jinja2.filters


def test_do_first_attributes():
    assert jinja2.filters.do_first.__name__ == 'sync_do_first'
    assert jinja2.filters.do_first.__qualname__ == 'jinja2.filters.do_first'"}
